WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:06.930
John B. Watson famously claimed that if he
were to be given a dozen healthy infants

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:12.900
he could shape them into anything:
doctors, lawyers, artists, beggars or

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:19.080
thieves, regardless of their background
or genetic predispositions. First he

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:24.180
completed experiments with eight-month
old Albert and later he applied his

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:29.640
theory when raising his own children. In
essence he applied the scientific method

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:35.460
to human psychology which he called
behaviorism. With the little Albert

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.000
experiment
Watson used the method of classical

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.789
conditioning to program a baby to be
afraid of a lab rat. Earlier Pavlov

00:00:44.789 --> 00:00:49.350
demonstrated how conditioning can
trigger biological responses that are

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:54.239
inherited genetically. Watson
hypothesized that we can also instill

00:00:54.239 --> 00:01:01.260
new behaviors that were not inherited. To
conduct the experiment Watson and his

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.360
assistant Rosalie Rayner placed the boy
in a room where a white rat was allowed

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.200
to roam around. First, the boy showed no
fear.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.810
Then Rayner struck a steel bar with a
hammer every time Albert reached out to

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:21.930
touch the rat, scaring Albert and causing
him to cry. Eventually, Albert tried to

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:26.250
get away from the rat showing that he
had been conditioned to fear the rat.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:31.920
Weeks later Albert showed distress
towards any furry object showing that

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:38.460
his conditioning had not only been
sustained but also generalized. Watson

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.950
assumed that our behavior is either a
reflex evoked by a stimulus or a

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:48.210
consequence of our individual history of
earlier exposure to reinforcements and

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:54.310
punishments paired with our current
motivational states and stimuli.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:59.510
Unlike Freud and Jung he was not
interested in thoughts or the mind

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:05.090
because in his opinion the analysis of
actions and reactions were the only way

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:09.649
to apply the scientific method to
psychology and get objective insights

00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:13.970
into human behavior.
He thought of psychology as an objective

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:20.990
branch of Natural Science, its goal the
prediction and control of behavior. Like

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:25.990
his fellow behaviorists he believed that
intelligence, temperament, and personality

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:32.570
are determined by the environment in
which the child is raised. Watson

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:38.270
published "the psychological care of
infant and child". In his book he advised

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:43.610
parents not to touch their children too
often and to keep an emotional distance so

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:48.320
as not to spoil them. Playing with
children, he warned, would interrupt their

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:55.459
routines. A happy child doesn't cry or
seek attention. His book became a

00:02:55.459 --> 00:03:00.350
best-seller and soon other scientists of
his time advised against showing

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:05.480
affection. Some Western governments
started to hand out leaflets advising

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:10.220
that parents should stop kissing their
children. Parents developed the idea that

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:14.959
children should be left to sit quietly
during the day at night, they should be

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:22.340
left crying alone until they fall asleep.
A method called sleep training. Watson

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:27.140
who had a difficult childhood wanted to
be a good father and applied his methods

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:33.950
to his four children John, Mary, James, and
William. Unfortunately things didn't turn

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:38.090
out as planned: John complained
throughout his entire life about

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:43.790
intolerable headaches and died early in
his 50s. Mary developed a drinking

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:49.040
problem and attempted suicide, like her
brother James. William took his own life

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:55.820
at age 40. Watson allegedly admitted that
he regretted writing about child-rearing

00:03:55.820 --> 00:04:01.130
as he realized he didn't know enough
about it to do so. Towards the end of his

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:06.050
life he became reclusive and prior to
his death in 1958

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:12.260
he burned all of his recent papers. What
do you think? Watson was convinced that

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:17.390
the kind of nurturing we receive can
determine our life path claiming that he

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:22.220
could turn an infant into any man he
wishes, in his own family though

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:28.100
depression and bad habits were passed on
from generation to generation. Does this

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:32.780
happen due to genetic predispositions or
is it the effect of a child's

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:36.160
unfortunate upbringing?

